        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "What data destruction standards do you follow for Bakersfield organizations?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "STS Electronic Recycling applies NIST SP 800-88 Rev. 2 media sanitization standards across all hard drives, solid-state disks, and storage media collected in Bakersfield. Our documented procedures help local healthcare, energy, and financial enterprises satisfy HIPAA 45 CFR §164.312, GLBA 16 CFR Part 314, and SOX 404 audit mandates with serialized certificates of destruction."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "Is electronics recycling pickup free for Bakersfield businesses?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Yes, STS provides complimentary pickup logistics for qualifying commercial volumes of computers, servers, networking hardware, and office electronics throughout Bakersfield and Kern County. Our logistics team handles secure loading, transport, and complete chain-of-custody tracking directly from your commercial site."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "How quickly can you schedule an ITAD pickup in Kern County?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Most commercial pickups in Bakersfield and surrounding Kern County communities are scheduled within three to five business days. We coordinate directly with facility managers and IT coordinators along Highway 99, Rosedale, and Stockdale corridors to ensure smooth, non-disruptive logistics."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "What happens to electronic equipment after collection in Bakersfield?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Collected equipment is securely staged and transported to our certified processing facilities in Jacksonville, Texas and Houston, Texas. Data-bearing components undergo permanent sanitization or shredding, while all remaining materials are processed through sustainable commodity recovery with zero landfill disposal."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "Do you provide electronics recycling for agricultural and energy operations in Bakersfield?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Yes, STS regularly serves Bakersfield's prominent agribusiness operators and energy extraction companies. We manage full disposition cycles for SCADA control systems, packaging line terminals, corporate workstations, and enterprise data center infrastructure with serialized tracking."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "How does STS ensure HIPAA compliance for healthcare providers in Bakersfield?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "STS provides HIPAA-compliant data destruction for Bakersfield healthcare networks and clinics. Every engagement includes formal Business Associate Agreements (BAAs), rigorous chain-of-custody documentation, and serialized certificates of destruction verifying complete ePHI sanitization under federal standards."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "Can Bakersfield companies recover value from retired IT assets?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Yes, our IT asset disposition program includes asset remarketing and liquidation services. Qualifying late-model enterprise laptops, servers, and networking hardware can be evaluated to return residual value to your organization, offsetting overall disposition and recycling costs."
